/// cross a threshold for one or more city-networks. Defines the
/// percentages, for performance scores or availability scores, that are the
/// local thresholds for when Amazon CloudWatch Internet Monitor creates a
/// health event. Also defines whether a local threshold is enabled or
/// disabled, and the minimum percentage of overall traffic that must be
/// impacted by an issue before Internet Monitor creates an event when a
/// threshold is crossed for a local health score. If you don't set a local
/// health event threshold, the default value is 60%. For more information,
/// see Change health event thresholds in the Internet Monitor section of
/// the CloudWatch User Guide .
pub struct LocalHealthEventsConfig {
  /// The status of whether Internet Monitor creates a health event based on a
  /// threshold percentage set for a local health score. The status can be
  /// ENABLED or DISABLED .
  pub status: Str? = None
  /// The health event threshold percentage set for a local health score.
  pub health_score_threshold: Float? = None
  /// The minimum percentage of overall traffic for an application that must
  /// be impacted by an issue before Internet Monitor creates an event when a
  /// threshold is crossed for a local health score. If you don't set a
  /// minimum traffic impact threshold, the default value is 0.1%.
  pub min_traffic_impact: Float? = None
}

